        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: أتقن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أتقن — atqana — \"to master\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أتقن جدي لغتين. atqana jaddī lughatayn. My grandfather mastered two languages."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يتقن, yutqin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أتقن (atqana) is built on the native Arabic root t-q-n, \"to do a thing skilfully\" (Lane). It is Form IV, to make a thing firm and exact: to master it. إتقان, mastery, is its verbal noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
